# Cloudflare Pages redirects — 301 duplicate/legacy URLs → canonical (consolidates SEO equity, kills duplicate content)
# Format:  /from   /to   301
# NOTE: on CF Pages, _redirects rules take precedence over static files at the same path, so a
# 301 fires even though the orphan .html still ships (see /index.html below). Deleting the orphan
# FILES is a separate SEO/Jason call (audit internal links first) — NOT required for these to work.

# Homepage = the Perch concierge shell. It iframes /home.html (a dedicated content
# copy) — NOT /index.html or / — so nothing the iframe loads can resolve back to the
# shell and nest it. Home links inside the iframe are redirected to /home.html by
/index.html              /                       301
/realestate.html         /real-estate       301
/taxation.html           /tax               301
/tax-controversies.html  /tax-controversy   301
/desclimer.html          /disclaimer        301
/the-cmm.html            /practice          301
/the-cmm2.html           /practice          301

# ---- 2026-08-11 (JAY-SEO-E1) — redirect targets are extensionless ----
# Every 301 above points at a CLEAN url, not a .html one. Cloudflare Pages already
# 308s /foo.html -> /foo, so a target ending in .html produced a two-hop chain:
#     /family-law.html -> 301 -> /experience.html -> 308 -> /experience
# Google follows chains but they dilute and they waste crawl budget, and an
# external audit reads the first hop's destination as the page's real content —
# which is how /family-law.html came to be reported as "a page about REIT IPOs".
# One hop now. Verified: every target below resolves 200 extensionless.

