# ---- added 2026-08-08 (JORDAN-196-LOGIN-SIGNOUT-R1, #196) — the Coming Soon orphan is gone ----
# login.html was a "Coming Soon" splash carrying the PREVIOUS site's nav (Clients /
# THE FIRM / THE PRACTICE) and no login of any kind. Real member authentication is
# the gate modal in js/members-gate.js, which opens off the four MEMBERS dropdown
# links and posts to /members/auth/signin. Shipping a page that says the member area
# is "coming soon" while the member area is live is the defect; the page is deleted.
#
# WHY 301 AND NOT 17 NAV EDITS. Seventeen legacy pages still spell the nav item
# `href="login.html"`. Repointing them means editing `nav.menubar` on each, which is
# the one region test/chrome-diff.test.mjs compares byte-for-byte and does NOT waive
# (`site-navigation` is outside REVIEWED_STRUCTURAL, which suppresses `page-structure`
# and nothing else). A redirect fixes all seventeen at the edge, with no page edited.
#
# BOTH SPELLINGS, per the /desclimer lesson above: CF Pages serves login.html at
# `/login` as well as `/login.html`, so an .html-only rule would leave the deleted
# file's canonical URL answering 404. Target is extensionless because /engagement
# self-canonicalises to the extensionless form.
#
# DESTINATION IS /engagement — the canonical MEMBERS page (JORDAN-MEMBERSHIP-CANONICAL,
# #43). It is in sitemap.xml, it describes the four levels, and it carries the MEMBERS
# dropdown whose GOLD / PLATINUM / DIAMOND / RESERVE links members-gate.js intercepts
# to open the sign-in card. That is the gate, reached the same way it is reached from
# every other page.
/login.html              /engagement             301
/login                   /engagement             301

