# ---- added 2026-07-24 (SHELDON-SEO-SITEMAP-CLEANUP, #68) ----
# The eight remaining .html-only dedup rules above had the same hole /desclimer had:
# CF Pages serves the extensionless URL straight from the file, so the .html rule
# 301s while the extensionless twin - which is the form sitemap.xml and every
# rel=canonical uses - kept serving duplicate content. The A1.1 SEO gate pinned all
# eight as known drift; these rules close them.
# Targets are extensionless because every destination page self-canonicalises to the
# extensionless URL (verified in-tree), so a .html target would 301 into a URL that
# immediately canonicalises away again. Destination PAGE is identical to the .html twin.
/business-formation      /entity-formation       301
