# ---- 2026-08-20 (voice-concierge removal + Vantage severance) ----
# `/  /perch.html  200` used to sit at the top of this file: a REWRITE that served the
# Perch concierge shell at the homepage while leaving the URL as `/`. The shell is
# deleted, so the rewrite is deleted with it and `/` now resolves to index.html — the
# real, indexable homepage. That is SHELDON-PERCH-A51's outcome reached by deletion
# instead of by a kill switch, which is why functions/_lib/perch-shell-retire.js is
# gone too.
#
# Four URLs stop having files behind them. Per the /desclimer and /login lessons above,
# BOTH spellings need a rule — CF Pages serves `/perch` from perch.html as readily as
# `/perch.html`, so an .html-only rule would leave the canonical form answering 404.
#
# /perch — the shell itself. It carried <meta name="robots" content="noindex"> and is
# in no sitemap, so Google should hold no copy; the 301 is for anyone holding the URL
# directly. It was the route the voice concierge connected on and it appears in old
# runbooks and PR descriptions.
#
# /home — a byte-copy of index.html that existed ONLY so the shell had something to
# iframe that could not resolve back to the shell and nest it. Nothing iframes anything
# now. It is not in sitemap.xml, but it answered 200 for months and may have been
# picked up, so it 301s rather than 404s.
#
# Target is `/` for all four: that is what both files were a copy or a wrapper of, and
# index.html already self-canonicalises there.
/perch.html              /                       301
/perch                   /                       301
/home.html               /                       301
/home                    /                       301

